// SURFACE-CACHE-0 (a design SPIKE, 2026-09-21) — THE CARD CAPTURE'S EXTRA
// G-BUFFER TARGETS, written from HlmsPbs with NO patch to the pin.
//
// WHAT THIS FILE IS MEASURING. The assessment (SPECS/SURFACE_CACHE_ASSESSMENT.md
// §8 item 5) records as UNVERIFIED whether a four-target capture from a PBS
// material can be written through the existing HlmsListener hooks or whether it
// needs a numbered patch. This file is the answer: it needs NO patch. Two hook
// pieces that upstream's own GLSL template inserts -- `custom_ps_output_types`
// (immediately after the built-in fragment outputs, so the running
// render-target-index counter keeps counting) and `custom_ps_posExecution` (inside main(), after
// DefaultBodyPS, where `pixelData` is still in scope because the body is a
// PIECE and not a function) -- plus one pass property set by our own
// HlmsListener are enough to add three more MRT attachments and fill them.
//
// THE PASS IS A PREPASS. `Ogre::PrePassCreate` already gives a capture two of
// the four channels a card wants, exactly and for free:
//
//     location 0  outNormals          the shading normal, *0.5+0.5
//     location 1  outShadowRoughness  x = THE SUN'S SHADOW TERM from the
//                                     shadow atlas, y = the GGX alpha
//
// and it computes no lighting at all, which is what makes a capture cheap. What
// it does NOT compute is the albedo (upstream skips SampleDiffuseMap in a
// prepass -- there is nothing in a prepass that wants it) or the emissive
// (computed inside the lit block). So this file adds:
//
//     location 2  outCardAlbedo       the diffuse albedo, linear
//     location 3  outCardEmissive     the emissive radiance
//     location 4  outCardDepth        VIEW-SPACE distance from the card plane,
//                                     in world units -- the depth test at the
//                                     read, and the one channel that makes a
//                                     card a surface rather than a decal
//
// ...and gets the albedo by inserting upstream's own SampleDiffuseMap at
// `custom_ps_posMaterialLoad`, which is after UnpackTextureIndices (the piece
// needs texIndex_diffuseIdx) and before the template's own gated insertion, so
// a capture samples it exactly once and a normal pass is untouched.
//
// SPELLED OUT AND NOT ABBREVIATED, because the Hlms parser reads directives
// inside comments (CLAUDE.md, lane SSR-1): there is no at-sign directive in any
// comment of this file. AND THE TRAP IS WIDER THAN THE RECORDED FORM — it is
// not only the block directives. `parseCounter` runs over a LIBRARY file's
// own text (the part outside every piece) before anything is generated, so a
// counter written in a COMMENT of a library file INCREMENTS THE REAL COUNTER:
// one such comment here, naming the render-target counter, shifted every
// fragment output location in the whole PBS shader by one and the scene
// rendered BLACK with nothing in any log. Measured on this lane, 2026-09-21.
//
// EVERY PIECE HERE IS INERT WITHOUT `jah_card_capture`, which only our listener
// sets and only while a capture workspace is executing. With it unset the
// generated shader is byte-identical to a build without this file -- which is
// what keeps both selftest hashes where they are.

// THE GUARD IS OUTSIDE THE PIECE, NOT INSIDE IT, and that is not style: the
// Hlms parser collects pieces at LIBRARY PARSE time and refuses a second
// definition of a name outright ("already defined"), which is a parse error
// that silently drops the OTHER file's piece for every permutation — the whole
// scene renders black. JahVct_piece_ps.any defines `custom_ps_posMaterialLoad`
// under its own property for the prepass-USE case, so both definitions are
// guarded and no permutation can ever see two.
@property( jah_card_capture )
@piece( custom_ps_output_types )
		#define outPs_cardAlbedo outCardAlbedo
		#define outPs_cardEmissive outCardEmissive
		#define outPs_cardDepth outCardDepth
		layout(location = @counter(rtv_target)) out vec4 outCardAlbedo;
		layout(location = @counter(rtv_target)) out vec4 outCardEmissive;
		layout(location = @counter(rtv_target)) out float outCardDepth;
@end
@end

// THE ALBEDO A PREPASS DOES NOT SAMPLE. Upstream gates SampleDiffuseMap on
// `!hlms_prepass || alpha_test || hlms_alpha_hash`; a capture wants it in a
// prepass, so it is inserted here -- once, and only under our property, so the
// alpha-tested case that ALREADY samples it does not sample it twice.
@property( jah_card_capture && hlms_prepass && !alpha_test && !hlms_alpha_hash )
@piece( custom_ps_posMaterialLoad )
		@insertpiece( SampleDiffuseMap )
@end
@end

@property( jah_card_capture )
@piece( custom_ps_posExecution )
		@property( hlms_normal || hlms_qtangent )
			outCardAlbedo = vec4( float3( pixelData.diffuse.xyz ), 1.0 );
			// THE EMISSIVE, recomputed rather than read: upstream accumulates it
			// straight into finalColour inside the lit block, so a prepass never
			// produces a value this could copy. The constant is the material's
			// own; the MAP is sampled the same way the lit block samples it.
			@property( emissive_map )
				outCardEmissive = vec4( float3( SampleEmissive(
						textureMaps@value( emissive_map_idx ),
						samplerState@value(emissive_map_sampler),
						UV_EMISSIVE( inPs.uv@value(uv_emissive).xy ),
						texIndex_emissiveMapIdx ).xyz )
					@property( emissive_constant ) * float3( material.emissive.xyz ) @end
					, 1.0 );
			@end
			@property( !emissive_map && emissive_constant )
				outCardEmissive = vec4( float3( material.emissive.xyz ), 1.0 );
			@end
			@property( !emissive_map && !emissive_constant )
				outCardEmissive = vec4( 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 );
			@end
			// Ogre's view space looks down -Z, so the distance from the capture
			// camera's plane is the negated view-space z. An ORTHOGRAPHIC
			// capture camera makes that a linear world-unit distance along the
			// card's own axis, which is exactly what the read depth-tests with.
			outCardDepth = -inPs.pos.z;
		@else
			outCardAlbedo = vec4( 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 );
			outCardEmissive = vec4( 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 );
			outCardDepth = 0.0;
		@end
@end
@end
